tion, beats everything.\n        13. Quadplex set: a quad with two single cards OR two pairs attached.\n        Use the EXACT card symbols provided in the Valid Moves list.\n        Prepare a valid JSON object like {"cards": ["♠3", "♥3"]} for your answer, along with your explanation and reason. If you pass, output: {"cards": []}\n        \n        Now is your turn, to your best ability, choose your move to maximize your chances of winning.\n        Please briefly evaluate a few proimsing moves, provide reason for your final choice, and output the action with specified format.\n        Your response format should be:\n        Evaluation: [Your Evaluation]\n        Reason: [Your Reason]\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\n    ', 'user_prompt': "You are playing as a peasant. Your aim is to be the play out all your cards before the landlord does, OR help your teammate (the other peasant) play out their cards before the landlord does. If the landlord plays out all cards first, you lose.\nYou are a Peasant. The Previous Player (Left) is the Landlord (ENEMY). The Next Player (Right) is your TEAMMATE (Peasant). You must cooperate with your teammate to beat the Landlord. The objective is to empty your hand before the landlord does, or help your teammate empty their hand before the landlord does.\n\nYour Hand: ♦4 ♠7 ♣8 ♣9 ♠Q ♣Q ♥K ♣K ♠A ♣A ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\nLast Play to Beat: None (Free Play)\n--- Game History (Recent) ---\nTurn 2 (You): Pass\nTurn 3 (Next Player): ♠6 ♥6 ♣6 ♦6\nTurn 3 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 3 (You): Pass\nTurn 4 (Next Player): ♦8 ♥9 ♦10 ♠J ♦Q\nTurn 4 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 4 (You): Pass\nTurn 5 (Next Player): ♥3 ♣3\nTurn 5 (Prev Player): ♠8 ♥8\nTurn 5 (You): ♣J ♦J\nTurn 6 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 6 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 6 (You): ♠3 ♦3\nTurn 7 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 7 (Prev Player): Pass\n--- Player Info ---\nCards Held by Next Player (Right) [Peasant (Teammate)]: 6\nCards Held by Prev Player (Left) [Landlord (Opponent)]: 7\n--- Cards Remaining Unknown (Card Counting) ---\n(Format explanation: 'Rank: Count', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\nRedJoker: 1, BlackJoker: 1, 2: 1, A: 1, K: 1, 10: 2, 9: 1, 7: 3, 5: 1, 4: 1\nValid Moves:\npair: ♠Q ♣Q\npair: ♥K ♣K\npair: ♠A ♣A\npair: ♠2 ♥2\npair_straight: ♠Q ♣Q ♥K ♣K ♠A ♣A\nsingle: ♦4\nsingle: ♠7\nsingle: ♣8\nsingle: ♣9\nsingle: ♠Q\nsingle: ♣K\nsingle: ♠A\nsingle: ♠2\ntriple: ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_pair: ♠Q ♣Q ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_pair: ♥K ♣K ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_pair: ♠A ♣A ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_single: ♦4 ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_single: ♠7 ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_single: ♣8 ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_single: ♣9 ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_single: ♠Q ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_single: ♣K ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\ntriple_with_single: ♠A ♠2 ♥2 ♦2\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': '**Okay, here\'s the plan. I\'m in a good spot. It\'s my turn, and I need to make the best play to help my team, and hopefully win. I\'ve got a killer hand.**\n\nI\'m the Peasant, and I\'m looking at my hand, and I see I\'m holding a really strong combination: `QQ KK AA`, three consecutive pairs. Also, I have a Triple: `222`. Looking at what’s been played, I know the counts on the cards, and I know the previous turns that are happening. I need to figure out the best way to leverage this. The Landlord has 7 cards left, and my teammate, the Next Player, has 6. If I make the correct move, I can set up a victory for the team.\n\nLet\'s do some card counting to look at remaining cards. I am looking at what has been played so far. I have a lot of pairs and triples. Okay, there are some unknowns in the deck, but I know what\'s in my hand, and I know what\'s been played. It\'s time to build a strategy. I know that bombs are a threat, and so is the Rocket (two Jokers). There’s no point in being timid here. I\'ve got to play aggressively to dominate the game.\n\nI’m looking closely at the cards still unknown. I know where the "big" cards are – the high singles, the Jokers, and the twos. Let\'s think through the best sequence. I am not seeing any bombs (4 of a kind), which is good, but I do need to consider the Rocket because that can ruin me. It is likely the Landlord has the Rocket. I have to play as though the Landlord has the Rocket, and make the play that either strips the Landlord\'s best defense, or that takes control of the board.\n\nMy strategy is to try and strip the Landlord of the Rocket or high cards, and then go out. I have two strong combinations in hand: `QQ KK AA`, and `222`, and a few singles. This is good. I need to find the best order to play them. If I play those pairs in sequence, can anyone beat them? No. I have the strongest combination of Pairs. This is perfect. I could play them separately, but that would be a waste. I also have the `222`, which is super strong. I also have a single `4` that I will need.\n\nSo, here\'s what I am going to do. The best play right now is to play this Pair Straight: `QQ KK AA`. This is a sequence of pairs and should force the Landlord to respond. They\'ll either have to play their Rocket, or pass. Either way, it\'s a win. If he uses the Rocket, then I’ve forced out the best weapon, and I have control to clear cards. If he passes, I play the Triple `222` and the `4`, and try to win with singles. I can strip his high cards if he has them. This move also leaves my teammate a chance.\n\nThis play is perfect. It\'s efficient, it\'s aggressive, and it puts me in the driver\'s seat. It will dominate the table and make it so the Landlord has to respond to me. This forces the best play that leads to a higher probability of winning.\n\nEvaluation: I possess a commanding hand with the highest possible Pair Straight (Queens, Kings, Aces) and a Triple of 2s. The Pair Straight is unbeatable except by a Rocket (Dual Jokers). Playing this 6-card combination allows me to clear a large portion of my hand with guaranteed control or force the Landlord to use their ultimate weapon (Rocket). This sets up my remaining hand (Triple 2s with a kicker) to likely clear or regain control, providing the best path to victory for the team.\n\nReason: The Pair Straight `QQ KK AA` is the "nuts" (highest possible) for its category, meaning no opponent can beat it with a normal hand. It forces the Landlord to either pass or use a Rocket. This move preserves my Triple 2s for the next turn and efficiently reduces my card count from 13 to 7, maintaining high pressure on the Landlord.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠Q", "♣Q", "♥K", "♣K", "♠A", "♣A"]}\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: I possess a commanding hand with the highest possible Pair Straight (Queens, Kings, Aces) and a Triple of 2s. The Pair Straight is unbeatable except by a Rocket (Dual Jokers) because I hold the top three ranks (Q, K, A) and the 2s. Playing this 6-card combination allows me to clear a large portion of my hand with guaranteed control or force the Landlord to use their ultimate weapon (Rocket). This sets up my remaining hand (Triple 2s with a kicker) to likely clear or regain control, providing the best path to victory for the team.\n\nReason: The Pair Straight `QQ KK AA` is the "nuts" (highest possible) for its category, meaning no opponent can beat it with a normal hand. It forces the Landlord to either pass or use a Rocket. This move preserves my Triple 2s for the next turn and efficiently reduces my card count from 13 to 7, maintaining high pressure on the Landlord.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠Q", "♣Q", "♥K", "♣K", "♠A", "♣A"]}'}
